SQLite Connection (db/connection.py)
pythonimport sqlite3, threading

_local = threading.local()

def get_conn(db_path: str) -> sqlite3.Connection:
    """Thread-local connection; WAL mode and FK enforcement applied once per thread."""
    if not hasattr(_local, 'conn') or _local.conn is None:
        conn = sqlite3.connect(db_path, check_same_thread=False, timeout=10)
        conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row
        conn.execute("PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL")
        conn.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON")
        conn.execute("PRAGMA synchronous=NORMAL")   # Safe with WAL; better performance
        _local.conn = conn
    return _local.conn
Why WAL matters here: The daemon writes every 60s; the Flask dashboard reads on every page load. With the default DELETE journal mode, reads block writes. WAL allows concurrent reads and one writer with no blocking.
